Nova's fixes to PptxGenJS 4.0.1 (MIT), applied by ../install.sh to dist/pptxgen.cjs.js (the
package "main") and dist/pptxgen.es.js ("module"). The browser bundles (bundle, min) are not used
in the Computer and are left as published. Each change is the upstream fix, ported from src/ to
the built files:

  1. gitbrent/PptxGenJS#1531, PR #1537: a category chart's embedded workbook wrote its table
     ref as "A1:C5'" (stray apostrophe). Keynote and Quick Look drop the whole chart when the
     workbook does not parse. The bubble chart's table ref also used the column count for its
     last row; it now uses the row count.
  2. PR #1540: 2D charts (bar, line, area, radar) listed a series axis id they never define,
     which makes PowerPoint offer to repair the file. Only BAR3D keeps its series axis.
  3. #1531, "secondary nit": a data value of 0 was written to the workbook as an empty cell
     (<v></v>) by "value || ''"; Edit Data showed a blank. It is now written as 0.

Remove this patch (and the grep marker in ../install.sh) when PptxGenJS ships all three.

